<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Venepal buys half of Colombia Packing.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Venepal buys half of Colombia Packing.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's paper and pulp manufacturer Venepal said it bought 50 percent of Colombia's Packing for $3.5 million.</p>
<p>The joint venture, Packing-Venepal, resulted from four years of study of the Colombian market, it said in a statement, and was made possible by the placement of Global Depositary Shares (GDS) for a total $12 million last November.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
</text>
